{
  "behaviorChanges": [
    "codex-run's implementation-review round budget is now a LADDER, not a wall. Rounds up to the adapter budget proceed; rounds up to budget+2 self-authorize with --allow-extra-rounds --extra-round-reason \"<reason>\" (>=12 chars, rubber stamps refused); past budget+2 refusal is absolute and says so. Previously any round past the budget was refused unconditionally and --allow-extra-rounds was never read on that path, which made the confirming round review-before-push mandates unreachable.",
    "A confirming round on an already-remediated diff is NOT charged against the budget. When every recorded round for the branch binds a diff hash other than the current one, the next round re-binds an owed verdict rather than funding new inquiry; codex-run prints codex_run_confirming_round: when the exemption applies. The exemption is bounded by the hard cap and fails closed whenever it cannot prove the prior rounds were voided.",
    "No refusal on the implementation-review round path can instruct an agent to consult a human, and each carries a runnable continuation. The previous message said \"split/defer/escalate\" and named no command.",
    "additive (adapter default): review.roundBudgets defaults move to {T0:0,T1:2,T2:3,T3:4}. T3 previously had no more rounds than T2, and T1=1 made the mandated confirming round illegal on the first finding. Explicit adapter pins are untouched."
  ],
